ball player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-17T20:09:26Z","intro":"Khalil Ja’Qua Bolden (born February 18, 2006) is an American college football safety for the Georgia Bulldogs of the Southeastern Conference (SEC).","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In his collegiate debut, Bolden recorded four tackles on 49 snaps, the most snaps of any Georgia defender, as the Bulldogs defeated Clemson 34–3."}]}}